WEBVTT

00:56.360 --> 00:59.581
Bronwyn? You here?

01:00.930 --> 01:02.801
I can't find my keys.

01:02.888 --> 01:04.542
Why is he still here?
Where's Sylvia?

01:04.586 --> 01:06.240
I don't know.

01:06.327 --> 01:08.242
Been trying
to reach her all morning.

01:08.329 --> 01:11.158
- Has he eaten?
- Uh, I ordered us some coffees

01:11.158 --> 01:13.377
from Balthazar
and I got him an eggs Benedict.

01:13.464 --> 01:14.944
- He wouldn't touch it.
- All right.

01:15.031 --> 01:18.034
- Hmm.

01:18.121 --> 01:20.471
Hey, Bash? Bud?

01:20.515 --> 01:24.780
Hey, can you, um,
can you try the bread?

01:24.823 --> 01:26.608
I don't like that.

01:26.695 --> 01:29.567
- Why not?
- It's bland.

01:29.611 --> 01:32.701
What-- Do you want me to put
something on it for you?

01:32.744 --> 01:35.225
Spicy curry mango?

01:37.401 --> 01:38.402
What?

01:53.417 --> 01:55.550
- Yeah? Okay.

01:55.593 --> 01:57.900
Keep eating, please.

02:10.565 --> 02:12.132
Mm.

02:12.132 --> 02:14.221
Oh, my God.

02:14.221 --> 02:16.571
Oh. How is that "slight pepper"?

02:16.614 --> 02:18.660
- Could you take him?

02:18.747 --> 02:21.706
I have to help Simon prep
a presentation before 9:00.

02:21.750 --> 02:25.145
I-- No, I... Oh, shit,
that stuff is really spicy.

02:25.145 --> 02:27.103
Oh, my God.

02:27.190 --> 02:29.410
- Fine. I already missed yoga.

02:29.453 --> 02:30.237
Mm.

02:32.456 --> 02:33.501
Hello?

02:34.850 --> 02:36.112
- Hey, Bash.
- Yes?

02:36.199 --> 02:38.419
I'll take you to school today.

02:38.462 --> 02:39.594
Really?

02:41.596 --> 02:42.466
Uh-huh.

02:44.033 --> 02:45.295
Uh-huh.

02:46.557 --> 02:47.819
Uh-huh.

02:47.863 --> 02:49.821
Eat, Bash.

02:49.821 --> 02:51.040
Uh-huh.

02:55.610 --> 02:57.960
- Of course.
- What is it?

02:59.918 --> 03:01.790
Of course.

03:12.844 --> 03:15.412
- Sylvia died.

03:18.110 --> 03:20.069
W-What, what happened? How?

03:20.156 --> 03:21.723
They don't know.

04:06.985 --> 04:08.987
Mom, where's Sylvia?

04:09.074 --> 04:10.946
Oh, honey, I already told you,

04:10.989 --> 04:13.949
she is not gonna make it today.

04:13.992 --> 04:15.646
Is she gonna pick me up?

04:15.690 --> 04:18.736
No, honey, Mommy or Daddy
will pick you up.

04:18.780 --> 04:20.782
But I want Sylvia.

04:20.869 --> 04:22.610
I know, honey.

04:25.700 --> 04:29.138
Are you sad because you missed
your yoga class?

04:30.792 --> 04:33.229
Do you need an ocean breath?

04:36.058 --> 04:38.103
Oh, honey.

04:46.764 --> 04:49.158
Everything is gonna be okay.

04:50.159 --> 04:51.291
Hugs.

04:56.339 --> 04:58.254
- Mommy?
- Yes, Bash?

04:58.341 --> 05:00.909
Sylvia walks me to my class.

05:02.127 --> 05:05.305
Oh. Okay.

05:20.232 --> 05:22.583
Hey, how was your day?

05:22.626 --> 05:26.021
Mm, it was okay.

05:26.064 --> 05:27.762
How was yours?

05:27.805 --> 05:30.634
- Fine, under the circumstances.
- Mm-hmm.

05:30.634 --> 05:33.594
You know, I gave
the doorman that envelope

05:33.637 --> 05:35.770
that was addressed to Sylvia.

05:35.770 --> 05:37.772
Told him return it to sender.

05:37.772 --> 05:40.035
He said he has no idea
who left it at our door.

05:40.078 --> 05:42.777
- Strange.
- It's weird, right?

05:42.777 --> 05:44.996
How's Sebastian doing?

05:45.040 --> 05:47.825
Good. Playing with that
coding thing you got him.

05:50.219 --> 05:53.744
Hey, you know,
his teacher asked me

05:53.788 --> 05:57.269
why we weren't at family
picture day, in front of him.

05:57.313 --> 06:00.360
What? I mean, we couldn't have
been the only parents.

06:00.360 --> 06:02.187
Right? I mean, seriously.

06:02.231 --> 06:04.102
It was ridiculous.

06:05.974 --> 06:07.584
So...

06:10.848 --> 06:12.633
...how do you want to
tell Bash

06:13.982 --> 06:18.073
Yeah, yeah, I was thinking
about that, too. Um...

06:18.116 --> 06:20.510
Do we want to tell him?

06:21.816 --> 06:23.295
Absolutely.

06:23.339 --> 06:24.862
I mean, we don't want
to lie to him.

06:24.906 --> 06:27.299
She was a really big part
of his life.

06:27.343 --> 06:28.823
If we don't say anything,

06:28.866 --> 06:30.825
he's gonna think death
is a bad thing.

06:30.868 --> 06:33.393
Well, it isn't the best thing.

06:34.829 --> 06:38.702
What did Dr. Lipschitz say
about teachable moments?

06:38.789 --> 06:40.530
You remember?

06:41.923 --> 06:43.272
Yeah, okay, I'll see you soon.

06:43.359 --> 06:44.882
All right. Bye.

06:44.926 --> 06:46.188
Bye.

06:59.941 --> 07:03.379
- Hey, Bash.
- Hey.

07:03.466 --> 07:05.686
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Hey.

07:05.729 --> 07:08.079
- Hey, buddy.

07:08.123 --> 07:10.691
- What you playing?
- Wow.

07:10.734 --> 07:12.867
Look at this.

07:12.867 --> 07:15.913
What's this one?

07:15.957 --> 07:20.309
That... This is a Kosmocertops.

07:20.396 --> 07:23.965
- Whoa. I love it.
- Wow.

07:24.052 --> 07:25.793
So cool.

07:29.927 --> 07:30.972
Hey, Bash.

07:33.757 --> 07:35.585
You remember that old dog

07:35.629 --> 07:38.283
- we used to have
when you were...
- Mm, no. Mm-mm, mm-mm.

07:39.415 --> 07:41.417
Well...

07:41.504 --> 07:43.637
you really love dinosaurs,
don't you, Bash?

07:45.290 --> 07:46.988
Uh, did you know

07:47.075 --> 07:51.427
that some things go extinct...

07:51.514 --> 07:54.343
- Yeah.
- ...like dinosaurs

07:54.386 --> 07:56.693
and woolly mammoths.

07:58.390 --> 08:00.262
Like, a meteor hit them?

08:00.305 --> 08:02.960
- Maybe.
- Mm-hmm.

08:03.004 --> 08:05.920
Yeah. Maybe.

08:05.963 --> 08:09.750
Or sometimes,

08:09.793 --> 08:13.928
they... might fall asleep

08:13.928 --> 08:15.625
and not wake up.

08:16.931 --> 08:18.933
Can that happen to me?

08:18.976 --> 08:21.196
- No. Mm-mm. No way.
- No. No.

08:21.239 --> 08:25.026
That only happens
when you're really old.

08:25.113 --> 08:27.942
Can that happen to you?

08:27.985 --> 08:31.293
- No. No, no, no, no.
- No, no, no. No.

08:31.293 --> 08:33.513
But you're both old.

08:39.127 --> 08:40.694
Sylvia died.

08:48.963 --> 08:52.967
Can she come back
and say goodbye

08:53.010 --> 08:56.057
and then go back to being dead?

08:57.406 --> 09:00.278
I don't think so, Bash.

09:00.365 --> 09:04.413
But sometimes, when people die,

09:04.456 --> 09:07.503
they have a special ceremony
to celebrate their life,

09:07.590 --> 09:09.070
and it's called a funeral.

09:09.157 --> 09:11.507
Can we go to there?

09:11.594 --> 09:13.857
- We can...
- Maybe. Maybe.

09:13.857 --> 09:17.426
Me and Daddy just need
to talk about it first.

09:17.513 --> 09:19.820
O-Okay?

09:27.392 --> 09:30.004
Maybe it's that foam roller?

09:30.047 --> 09:31.353
I'll check.

09:31.353 --> 09:33.877
- Mm-hmm.
- Where did she go?

09:35.879 --> 09:37.838
Oh...

09:37.881 --> 09:40.884
Nobody knows, baby.

09:40.884 --> 09:45.889
Maybe Sylvia went back
to Trinidad and Tobago.

10:19.314 --> 10:21.098
I just never realized
how many things

10:21.142 --> 10:23.318
she had lying around the house.

10:23.361 --> 10:27.061
I mean, bags...

10:27.104 --> 10:30.412
...wigs, dresses.

10:30.455 --> 10:33.110
We'll contact her family.

10:34.895 --> 10:36.636
We should've hired
somebody younger.

10:36.636 --> 10:39.639
Yeah, you know, hon?

10:41.641 --> 10:43.207
I think we should take him.

10:45.949 --> 10:49.300
No, that-- It is,
it is too jarring for a kid

10:49.300 --> 10:52.042
- in kindergarten.
- Okay, listen.

10:52.086 --> 10:54.088
I thought about it.

10:54.088 --> 10:57.352
I think this could be
a real teachable moment.

10:57.395 --> 10:59.746
I mean, he said
he wanted to see her.

10:59.746 --> 11:02.052
- I think we should
honor his wishes.

11:02.096 --> 11:06.100
You know, I was reading about
how we as Americans

11:06.100 --> 11:08.842
have commodified death
to the point

11:08.929 --> 11:12.149
where it's become this, like,
foreign, scary thing.

11:12.193 --> 11:14.630
I mean, it used to be
that the living room--

11:14.717 --> 11:16.545
the living room, in your house--

11:16.632 --> 11:18.982
used to be the death room.

11:19.069 --> 11:21.245
I mean, it's where you would
house the body

11:21.289 --> 11:24.640
of the dead person and people
would come and go for days

11:24.727 --> 11:28.426
just to, just to look
at-at the dead person.

11:30.428 --> 11:31.821
Ew.

11:37.087 --> 11:38.567
I'm gonna call her phone.

11:40.743 --> 11:43.267
Maybe we can return these things
to her family in person.

11:46.227 --> 11:48.882
I think her daughter said
the service starts at 10:00 a.m.

11:48.969 --> 11:51.580
I don't know.
It was hard to understand her.

11:51.667 --> 11:54.365
Maybe this next person

11:54.452 --> 11:59.370
can be a bit more...

11:59.414 --> 12:01.329
metropolitan.

12:03.200 --> 12:05.507
Mm-hmm.

12:05.507 --> 12:08.031
Sounds expensive.

12:08.118 --> 12:10.033
Sylvia wasn't cheap.

12:10.120 --> 12:13.558
No. Sylvia wasn't expensive.

12:17.040 --> 12:19.173
Babe, you know
what would be so great?

12:19.173 --> 12:21.218
- Hmm?
- If Sebastian

12:21.262 --> 12:23.612
could become fluent in Mandarin.

12:25.396 --> 12:30.227
Look, you know how hard it is to
find a Chinese nanny right now.

12:30.271 --> 12:31.576
Why? No, you're just not asking
the right people.

12:31.620 --> 12:33.665
You don't know where to look.

12:33.709 --> 12:35.450
If you want him to be
in business, he needs to learn

12:35.493 --> 12:36.973
the language of busin--

12:38.192 --> 12:40.498
I'm scared.

12:40.585 --> 12:43.414
Oh, you were so quiet,
Sebastian.

12:43.414 --> 12:45.939
I didn't, I didn't
see you, baby.

12:46.026 --> 12:50.247
Sylvia sits in my room
when I'm scared.

12:50.291 --> 12:53.424
Sometimes she rubs my back.

12:59.213 --> 13:00.954
In a circle.

13:08.222 --> 13:12.574
And then, she sits
in the rocking chair and sings

13:12.574 --> 13:16.360
the "Sweet T and T" song.

13:16.360 --> 13:18.232
What?

13:24.238 --> 13:28.242
Oh, um, well,
I don't know that song.

13:28.285 --> 13:30.287
But I do know...

13:49.306 --> 13:53.528
We're all here
and we are all safe.

13:53.571 --> 13:56.052
So you don't have to worry.

13:57.706 --> 13:59.795
I feel worried.

14:03.625 --> 14:05.627
Well, that is okay.

14:22.252 --> 14:23.471
You okay, Bash?

14:26.300 --> 14:29.172
Yep. We are out there.

14:29.259 --> 14:32.523
Hmm. Practically in the islands.

14:38.399 --> 14:41.315
Hi, guys. Hi.

14:41.358 --> 14:43.621
Uh, we're looking
for Sylvia Hosannah's funeral.

14:43.708 --> 14:46.276
Is it... Is this it?

14:46.320 --> 14:49.410
- Are you Miles?
- I am.

14:49.497 --> 14:51.194
Yeah, we met on the phone.
I'm Khadija.

14:51.281 --> 14:54.154
- Sylvia's daughter.
- Oh, really nice to meet you.

14:54.197 --> 14:56.069
- Our condolences.
- Thank you so much.

14:56.156 --> 14:59.072
She was so much a part
of our son's life.

14:59.159 --> 15:00.595
- Oh, I know.
- Yeah.

15:00.638 --> 15:02.292
You know, we-we have

15:02.336 --> 15:04.642
some of her belongings here
from our apartment.

15:04.686 --> 15:06.383
- We want to make sure
we get those to you today.
- Oh.

15:06.427 --> 15:08.559
Oh, yeah.
Great, thank you so much.

15:08.603 --> 15:09.560
Cockroach.

15:09.604 --> 15:12.346
Richard. Stop it.

15:12.389 --> 15:14.565
Trust me, it's not
as bad as it sounds.

15:14.609 --> 15:17.394
"Cockroach has no place
at fowl party."

15:17.438 --> 15:20.615
A'A, and I bet you know
what that means.

15:20.658 --> 15:23.226
- You must be Sebastian.

15:23.313 --> 15:25.620
Mommy used to call you
her little curry mouth

15:25.663 --> 15:28.231
because you love her roti
and ate it plenty.

15:28.318 --> 15:32.366
I heard so much
about you, all of you.

15:32.366 --> 15:36.544
So all are staying
for the wake later, right?

15:36.631 --> 15:40.200
Yes, we is family now, and you
have to stay for the wake later.

15:40.243 --> 15:41.853
Right? And you'll have
plenty food.

15:41.897 --> 15:43.812
It will have pelau, corn soup,

15:43.812 --> 15:48.077
fish broth, doubles, roti.

15:48.121 --> 15:50.036
And as Mommy used to say,
it's better belly bust...

15:50.036 --> 15:52.125
...than good food waste.

15:53.822 --> 15:55.389
- You know me heart.
- A'A.

15:55.389 --> 15:58.827
- But it's a little
Trini all here?

15:58.914 --> 16:01.525
- Wow...
- Oh, my gosh.

16:01.569 --> 16:04.267
Thank you so much, Sebastian.
You made me laugh today.

16:04.354 --> 16:06.617
- Thank you.
- That's great.

16:06.617 --> 16:09.707
Um, so c-- am I okay here?

16:09.794 --> 16:12.710
- Can I pull...
- Oh, just follow me,
I'll show you where to park.

16:12.797 --> 16:15.191
- Oh, I'll take Sebastian out
and wait for you.
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

16:23.983 --> 16:25.985
Great.

16:25.985 --> 16:27.247
Um...

16:29.510 --> 16:32.687
Am I gonna be able to, uh,
like, get out of here?

16:32.730 --> 16:34.428
Oh, yeah, yeah, just rest
the car keys on the hood

16:34.428 --> 16:35.907
and Richie will
take care of you.

16:35.951 --> 16:38.084
- Oh, okay.
- Mm-hmm. Richie.

16:41.609 --> 16:44.003
All right. Okay.

16:44.003 --> 16:45.004
Hi, Richie.

16:47.528 --> 16:50.096
Hi, Richie.

16:50.096 --> 16:52.402
- Hi... Okay.
- It's fine. It's fine.

17:05.328 --> 17:07.461
- Thank you.
- Thank you. I'm good, thanks.

17:10.333 --> 17:12.814
Okay. Hey.

17:12.814 --> 17:14.598
Take my hand.

17:29.570 --> 17:32.268
I'm gonna lift you up
so you can see, okay?

17:40.929 --> 17:42.191
Okay?

17:45.890 --> 17:48.806
Good job, buddy.
Let's go find a seat.

17:54.986 --> 17:57.554
Excuse me. Can we take these?
Thank you.

17:57.598 --> 17:59.774
- Thank you.
- You sit here.

17:59.817 --> 18:01.515
I'll sit next to you.

18:04.692 --> 18:06.433
Good job, bud.

18:11.525 --> 18:14.528
Hey, y'all must be the Warners.

18:14.571 --> 18:16.660
Sylvia did love your family.

18:16.704 --> 18:18.749
She really did.

18:18.793 --> 18:20.969
I'm glad you're all here.

18:20.969 --> 18:22.579
My condolences and thank you.

18:22.623 --> 18:24.581
You're her brother?

18:24.625 --> 18:26.453
Nah, her comparé.

18:26.453 --> 18:27.932
Oh.

18:27.976 --> 18:29.760
My name is Devon.

18:29.760 --> 18:31.980
Now, if you guys
are in the market

18:32.023 --> 18:34.852
for a new childcare service,

18:34.939 --> 18:37.246
I'd like to offer my assistance.

18:37.290 --> 18:39.422
I-I've been
a Little League coach,

18:39.509 --> 18:41.859
spiritual therapist

18:41.946 --> 18:44.514
and I install televisions
when I can.

18:44.558 --> 18:47.430
- Wow.
- Just hit my line.

18:47.517 --> 18:49.519
You don't have shame?

18:49.563 --> 18:51.347
Know your place.

18:57.527 --> 18:59.790
Hey. Psst.

18:59.834 --> 19:01.575
My name's Curtis.

19:01.618 --> 19:04.621
Hi. Miles. Hi.

19:04.665 --> 19:06.623
Uh, this is my wife and son.

19:06.667 --> 19:08.451
Yeah, man, nice to meet you.

19:08.538 --> 19:10.105
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

19:11.933 --> 19:14.065
So, how you know Sylvia?

19:14.109 --> 19:16.720
Well, Sylvia used
to care for Sebastian.

19:16.764 --> 19:18.635
Oh, serious?

19:18.679 --> 19:21.595
You know, Sylvia was
my babysitter, too. Ha.

19:21.638 --> 19:23.814
- Wow.
- Yeah, it's a sad day.

19:23.858 --> 19:26.469
- But she'd be happy
we're all here, you know.
- Yeah.

19:28.689 --> 19:32.649
So, um, you grow up in Trinidad?

19:32.693 --> 19:33.911
Or Jamaica?

19:33.998 --> 19:36.479
No, it's Trinidad and Tobago.

19:36.566 --> 19:38.829
And no.

19:38.829 --> 19:41.441
I'm from Tribeca.

19:41.484 --> 19:46.576
Oh. Your-your accent
is so... strong.

19:46.620 --> 19:48.491
Yeah, everyone says that.

19:50.058 --> 19:52.930
Sorry I'm late.

19:53.017 --> 19:56.282
As they say,
any time is Trini time, eh?

19:56.282 --> 19:58.501
- Let the church say "amen."

19:58.588 --> 20:00.503
Amen.

20:00.590 --> 20:03.114
Welcome to the homegoing service

20:03.158 --> 20:06.901
of the beloved
Sylvia Lucille Hosannah.

20:06.944 --> 20:09.338
Bow your head
and close your eyes.

20:10.992 --> 20:13.081
Psalm 34:18 says,

20:13.081 --> 20:16.040
"God is close
to the brokenhearted...

20:16.127 --> 20:19.914
- Yes.
- ...and loves those
who are crushed in spirit."

20:19.957 --> 20:21.959
- Yes.
- That mean,

20:22.046 --> 20:24.658
even if you may not
feel his presence,

20:24.658 --> 20:26.660
the Lord is close to you.

20:26.660 --> 20:28.401
- Yes.
- Yes, Lord.

20:28.488 --> 20:30.098
And if the Lord is close to you,

20:30.185 --> 20:32.535
Sylvia is close to you, amen?

20:32.622 --> 20:34.972
- Amen.
- Let the church say amen, amen?

20:35.059 --> 20:36.626
- Amen.
- Let me just say "amen."

20:36.670 --> 20:38.149
Amen.

20:38.193 --> 20:39.760
- Amen.
- We have
come here today

20:39.847 --> 20:42.502
to celebrate the marvelous life

20:42.545 --> 20:45.374
of Ms. Sylvia Lucille Hosannah.

20:45.418 --> 20:46.680
- Oh, yeah.
- Born in Trinidad

20:46.723 --> 20:50.727
on June the 8th
in the year 1957.

20:50.771 --> 20:53.687
She is survived
by her beautiful children,

20:53.687 --> 20:59.562
Princess Lee, Khadija Lee,
her son Steven Lee Jr.

20:59.649 --> 21:03.958
and her grandchildren
Wesley and Zachary.

21:04.001 --> 21:06.787
She was a passionate
childcare professional.

21:06.874 --> 21:07.962
- Yes! Yes!
- Yes.

21:08.005 --> 21:10.965
A nanny and nurse
to many, many children

21:11.008 --> 21:14.185
right here in New York City.

21:14.229 --> 21:16.579
And she always
loved children, eh?

21:16.666 --> 21:18.799
But she didn't just take
care of children, right?

21:18.886 --> 21:20.453
No.

21:20.540 --> 21:23.934
Before settling down
and having children of her own,

21:23.978 --> 21:26.589
she was a ballet dancer
with the Alvin Ailey

21:26.676 --> 21:28.939
dance company in Harlem
for several years.

21:29.026 --> 21:30.985
Yes.

21:31.028 --> 21:34.728
Mixing Trinidadian
and traditional African dance,

21:34.771 --> 21:38.166
she brought a confidence
and a freshness

21:38.209 --> 21:40.690
to her rich and vibrant
dance milieu.

21:40.734 --> 21:43.258
- Yes.
- Oh, yeah.

21:43.345 --> 21:45.739
Sylvia was the first in her
family to move from Trinidad

21:45.782 --> 21:49.308
to New York and always
sent money to her family.

21:57.925 --> 22:02.103
She tried her best to get
all her brothers and sisters

22:02.103 --> 22:04.758
to the U.S. as well.

22:04.801 --> 22:07.630
- Including her sister Nancy,

22:07.717 --> 22:10.633
whose son Oswald
is doing his thing

22:10.720 --> 22:12.766
as wide receiver
for the Patriots!

22:15.812 --> 22:17.205
Except last week.

22:17.292 --> 22:20.251
Sad as he lost me
some money, boy.

22:20.295 --> 22:22.863
Oswald James was
related to our nanny?

22:22.950 --> 22:26.823
- Yeah, I heard.
- She will be
extremely missed.

22:26.867 --> 22:30.914
God deals with death
as he knows it to be true.

22:30.914 --> 22:34.657
Isaiah 41:10 says,

22:34.744 --> 22:37.356
"Fear not, for I am with you.

22:37.356 --> 22:39.009
- Yes.
- Yes.

22:39.053 --> 22:40.097
"Be not dismayed,

22:40.184 --> 22:42.056
- "for I am your God.
- Yes.

22:42.099 --> 22:44.101
- "I will strengthen you.
- Yes.

22:44.188 --> 22:46.321
- "I will help you.
- Yes.

22:46.408 --> 22:48.802
"I will uphold you
with my righteous hand!

22:48.845 --> 22:51.631
- Yes.

22:52.980 --> 22:54.373
With my righteous hand."

22:55.809 --> 22:56.810
Yes.

22:56.853 --> 22:58.115
And she is upheld

22:58.202 --> 23:00.466
with His righteous hand.

23:00.466 --> 23:03.338
And she is with God,
sitting where?

23:03.425 --> 23:05.209
- At the right...
- At the right hand
of the Father.

23:06.994 --> 23:08.822
- May she rest in peace.
- What was that?

23:08.822 --> 23:10.345
Uh, nothing. Nothing.

23:10.432 --> 23:12.913
And may God bless
her sweet, sweet soul.

23:14.175 --> 23:15.916
All right, that done.

23:16.003 --> 23:21.487
Now, as per the deceased
Mrs. Hosannah's wishes,

23:21.487 --> 23:23.837
we are asked
to celebrate her life.

23:23.880 --> 23:26.883
I think one thing
we can all say about Sylvia,

23:26.927 --> 23:28.972
is that she believed
in tradition...

23:30.713 --> 23:32.367
...but she was
not at all traditional.

23:32.454 --> 23:34.717
- This is true.

23:34.804 --> 23:37.285
She asked that there
be limbo dance,

23:37.372 --> 23:39.809
in tribute to Julia Edwards,

23:39.853 --> 23:42.899
before being taken
to the burial site.

23:42.943 --> 23:44.814
We have some students
and alumni here

23:44.858 --> 23:46.425
from the Hillcrest High School

23:46.512 --> 23:49.732
after-school dance program--
started by Sylvia, by the way--

23:49.819 --> 23:53.562
to help us fulfill
this ask of Mrs. Hosannah.

23:53.606 --> 23:57.827
We will also be playing
one of Sylvia's favorite songs,

23:57.871 --> 24:01.135
- "Trini 2 De Bone."
- Yes!

24:01.178 --> 24:06.619
So, if all you could please
join us in remembering Sylvia

24:06.706 --> 24:09.448
in the way that she wanted
to be remembered.

24:10.884 --> 24:12.755
Yes. Amen. Amen.

24:12.842 --> 24:14.061
- There we go, now.

25:24.958 --> 25:26.176
- All yah!

25:26.176 --> 25:29.397
Stop all of this bacchanal.
Stop it!

25:29.397 --> 25:31.965
- How-how she
reach up there?

25:31.965 --> 25:33.967
- Here we go.
- Everyone here

25:34.010 --> 25:36.404
- loved this woman.
- Princess!

25:36.404 --> 25:39.842
I've heard about her sacrifices,
her selflessness,

25:39.929 --> 25:42.628
but who do you think
she sacrificed, hmm?

25:42.671 --> 25:45.239
To take care
of those children, hmm?

25:45.282 --> 25:46.936
- She did the best
she could, Princess.
- Yeah?

25:46.980 --> 25:50.810
Where was she
when we needed her, Steven?

25:50.853 --> 25:52.725
Where was she when you got
jumped uptown,

25:52.812 --> 25:54.683
and I couldn't find you
for a whole day?

25:56.293 --> 25:58.208
Where was she
when they broke into our house

25:58.295 --> 26:00.428
and stole my laptop?

26:00.515 --> 26:02.952
Where was she?

26:02.996 --> 26:05.346
Where was she
at your finals, Steven?

26:05.389 --> 26:07.740
She was providing for us.

26:07.827 --> 26:09.002
She was with other people's
children.

26:09.002 --> 26:10.743
She should've been
taking care of her own!

26:10.830 --> 26:13.572
That's enough, Princess. Stop.

26:13.572 --> 26:17.010
I needed you, Mommy.

26:17.010 --> 26:18.838
And where were you?!

26:20.056 --> 26:22.450
Where were you?! Huh, Mama?!

26:22.450 --> 26:24.713
You've always been crazy,
Princess!

26:24.757 --> 26:26.019
Hey, but what you
really doing here?

26:26.062 --> 26:27.890
- A'A?
- A'A?

26:30.980 --> 26:31.894
Whoa.

26:33.896 --> 26:35.245
It's a church! Stop!

26:37.204 --> 26:39.989
I'm coming with you!

26:41.208 --> 26:43.514
Stop it! Stop!

26:43.558 --> 26:46.300
Worldstar! Worldstar!
There's a fight going down...

26:46.343 --> 26:48.868
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey! Hey!

26:48.911 --> 26:53.089
Hey! You all need
to calm down right now!

26:53.133 --> 26:55.352
Look, you're scaring
the white people.

26:58.007 --> 26:59.922
Uh... No, no, no, no.

27:00.009 --> 27:03.099
No, uh...

27:03.143 --> 27:05.319
We just have to go.

27:05.362 --> 27:08.844
Hey, small man.
Are we scaring you?

27:11.455 --> 27:13.283
It's okay.

27:13.370 --> 27:15.242
We're just sad.

27:17.505 --> 27:21.770
This... is how we're sad.

27:58.328 --> 28:00.983
- You okay, Bash?
- Yes.

28:00.983 --> 28:05.118
Well, if you want to sleep
with us, you can.

28:05.161 --> 28:07.250
I'm okay.

28:07.250 --> 28:11.124
Okay. All right.

28:11.211 --> 28:14.127
Well...

28:14.170 --> 28:16.477
Well, good night.

28:16.477 --> 28:18.479
I love you.

28:18.522 --> 28:20.568
Good night. I love you, Dad.

28:30.143 --> 28:31.710
Good night, Sylvia.

28:43.156 --> 28:45.506
Wow.

28:45.549 --> 28:48.161
Oh, my gosh.

28:48.161 --> 28:51.294
Hey, hon, you know the origin
of the limbo dance?

28:51.294 --> 28:53.035
It's fascinating.

28:53.122 --> 28:55.037
I mean, apparently,

28:55.124 --> 28:59.041
slaves would do it to mimic
going down in the hold

28:59.128 --> 29:01.174
- of a slave ship.
- Did we do the right thing?

29:01.217 --> 29:02.566
What?

29:04.220 --> 29:07.136
Of course we did.

29:07.180 --> 29:08.877
Well, I just...

29:10.183 --> 29:13.752
I mean, people were screaming.

29:13.795 --> 29:17.190
- And-and the way that
that woman was yelling...
- All right, that...

29:17.233 --> 29:20.236
...at her mother.

29:20.280 --> 29:25.851
I just, I never... want
Sebastian to feel that way.

29:25.851 --> 29:28.244
- Like we weren't there for him.
- No.

29:28.288 --> 29:33.859
We were there for him today,
when he needed us.

29:33.902 --> 29:36.209
We were there for him.
We are there for him.

29:36.209 --> 29:39.255
Look, I know Sebastian,
and I know

29:39.299 --> 29:41.431
that he can handle
what he saw today.

29:41.431 --> 29:43.172
I know he'll be fine.

29:54.880 --> 29:59.232
You know, when I was putting
Sebastian to bed tonight,

29:59.275 --> 30:03.453
I asked him, "What do you want
to be when you grow up?"

30:03.453 --> 30:08.981
and he said, "I want to play
steelpan like Uncle Samuel."

30:13.420 --> 30:14.813
I don't even...

30:16.423 --> 30:19.469
Honey, wha... U-Uncle Samuel?

30:19.469 --> 30:22.298
I don't know what that is.
Who's Uncle Samuel?

30:22.342 --> 30:25.084
- I don't know.
- Was he there today?

30:25.127 --> 30:26.172
I don't know.
